---
description: Versioned capture integrity and bounded compatibility loading (#337, ungated #320)
globs: backend/capture/**,backend/sim/capture_*.py
alwaysApply: false
---

# Capture fidelity (ADR 001, ADR 017)

- Capture owns manifest/JSONL schema version 1. Session rotation invalidates write
  state; schema changes require explicit migration. Missing versions and the known
  sim_capture_v1 label migrate in memory after row validation; unknown versions
  and malformed manifests refuse selection/resume loudly.
- Validate timestamps before writing and before print aggregation. A backward
  event timestamp fails the recording, retaining the already accepted prefix.
  Date rollover finalizes the old directory then resumes the row's Eastern date.
  Stream bar timestamps may equal an earlier partial bucket on resume.
- Sample L2 in event time, retain the newest pending update, and flush the final
  book on stop. Persist offered/coalesced counters with the effective rate limit.
- Daily buckets use the session opening hour on the event's own calendar date;
  pre-open events belong to the previous session anchor. Emit only at rollover
  or final flush. Compatibility replay does not read unused daily bar files.
- Compatibility loading counts malformed, invalid timestamp and invalid payload
  rows. Bounded L2 decimation preserves the first/final book and exposes both
  total and loaded counts. These diagnostics travel in replay_load.
- Default storage is F:/Nova/sim_capture when available, otherwise the user's
  local application-data directory (or XDG data directory on Unix), never the
  checkout cache. An explicit NOVA_SIM_CAPTURE_DIR override remains authoritative.
- Retention and delete controls remain operator-gated under #320.
- Selection builds an immutable data snapshot off-lock, then publishes it only if its generation is current. Clear/new selection invalidates pending loads. Capture locks never call historical selection/status functions; the feed is suppressed while capture selection is loading.
- Capture quote/book/ticker projections expose only recorded facts. Missing bid/ask, size, prior close, depth, daily/minute bars and trade fields remain null/empty; before first event, while loading, or after failure, never substitute synthetic data (there is no synthetic instrument -- ADR 019). Quote/book/snapshot projection lives in sim/market_views.py under ADR 001.
- Clock alignment during capture publication uses notify=False: no tape/depth fanout or replay/history lookup may execute under the capture lock. After release, a generation-fenced rebuild pins one capture snapshot. Quote and ticker projections likewise share one pinned snapshot across all field reads.
- Capture latest_quote follows SnapshotData: bid_price/ask_price/bid_size/ask_size are recorded numbers or null, plus timestamp; legacy bid/ask aliases remain for compatibility. No unknown size is replaced with a default.
